Chloropomp

Ingredients: ELECTRONIC BODY MUSIC (EBM) + SYNTHPOP & NEW ROMANTICS + CINEMATIC, Epic & ORCHESTRAL + Fiddle + 2000s ERA
Creative Catalyst: Its founding artists were botanists who sonified the electrical signals of rainforest plants.

Chloropomp sounds like an aristocratic ballroom staged inside a flooded biodome during an industrial blackout: brutal, synchronized 16th-note EBM bassline stomps collide violently with sweeping early-2000s cinematic brass, drenched in flamboyant New Romantic vocal melodrama and lightning-fast, rosin-shredding fiddle lines triggered by the micro-volt surges of weeping epiphytes.

Genre DNA
- Tempo & Pulse: 132–140 BPM; relentless, mechanized 4/4 body-stomp kicks locked into jackhammer EBM sequences, periodically pulled into erratic, organic micro-swings dictated by bio-electric voltage shifts.
- Harmonic Palette: Dramatic Dorian and harmonic minor arrangements laced with 19th-century Wagnerian chromatic modulations, suspended over dissonant, plant-generated microtonal drones.
- Production Signatures:
  1. Phloem-Sidechain Compression: Rhythmic ducking of massive GigaStudio-era orchestral brass sections triggered by the sudden millivolt spikes of punctured jungle foliage.
  2. Glasshouse Convolution: Running shrill, virtuoso fiddle flourishes through custom impulse responses of humid, glass-domed Victorian conservatories and cavernous industrial storm drains.
  3. Millennium Overdrive Layering: Hyper-compressed 2000s virtual-analog supersaws saturated through gritty German rackmount preamps, blurring the line between synthetic brass and screaming plant circuitry.
- Dynamics: Monumental, opera-scaled crescendos that abruptly drop out into intimate, humid field recordings of soil dripping onto contact mics, before detonating into wall-of-sound rhythmic battery.

